  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2025 Regional DREF WASH ops Review</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This review seeks to enhance the quality and sustainability of Emergency WASH interventions in Africa by analysing DREF-supported activities. It will examine the relevance of interventions to local needs, assess their effectiveness in achieving intended outcomes, and identify elements that can support longer-term resilience programming. By reviewing operational demand, National Society capacity, and lessons learned, the review will generate actionable insights to guide future planning, capacity development, and strategic decision-making. This nine-month review, led by the IFRC Africa regional WASH team, NLRC and selected National Societies, will identify the types of disasters prompting WASH interventions, assess their scale, and evaluate NS capacity in water, sanitation, and hygiene promotion. Methods include a desk review, online interviews, and field visits to selected countries.</narrative>
  </description>
